here you can access it like a nine  palace to start bridging seemingly  different data areas to get better  insights  new insights well that's really exciting  Tilly and it is you know I still  mentioned this is aspirational if you  will but actually we're a long way  towards that now the technologies are  actually there now it's a matter of  changing the behaviors and putting the  energy into this transformation this  digitalization so it's really it's  exciting it's aspirational but you know  you have to aspire to something in order  to get to the next level so another  thing that comes out of this data 360  who becomes essentially part of it if  you will is this concept of situational  awareness and I go back to the concept  of the Blue Angels they have this out  this helmet on that gives them a  360-degree view of everything that's  going on around those planes they have  dashboards that give them status  information on the flight platform that  they're flying and they have threat  detection built right in so they get  alerts and they have predictive  information that tells them something  about the future and prescriptive  information that tell are prescriptive  algorithms that tell them about things  that can maybe help them defend  themselves so this kind of you know  situational awareness applies to the  research lab believe it or not because  we don't want our researchers walking  around with helmets like that much  rather have them you know looking like  researchers and acting like researchers  but we can give them this 360 degree  view with this situational awareness  using informatics platforms that are  capturing the data in real time and this  is what we're doing with the case study  that we provided you know they can  actually get at the data have a  360-degree view  sit down and a platform and know exactly  what's going on in the research lab  who's doing what kind of work when and  what the statuses of those that work and  if there's problems that arise we are  building systems now with IOT devices so  that we can actually monitor the  environmental health or monitor the  health of freezers and have  anomaly detection algorithms which we  are running now which actually can  detect problems maybe before they become  serious problems send an alert so that  those problems can be resolved and then  predictive or predictive information  about what's gonna happen in the future  so if you see this anomaly happening in  a voltage stream on a freezer for  example you might know that that freezer  is about to fail and you have some  predictive information to help guide you  to a better a better outcome so all of  these things are happening now and  they're happening now because of the  cloud it's one of the technologies that  have transformed all of this in fact  this isn't really the core technology  that's transformed and brought us to  this time where we have digitalization  and in this view here you can see we  have these Data Platform  with different panels of data all  aggregated and views mobile devices so  that you can actually find the data  while you are on the subway if you want  you can actually look at your data but  you can the data you are born mobile now  with these devices there's the systems  and the data are aggregated harmonized  and searchable so that's where we are  making progress right now we've solved  this problem in a lot of areas so now we  come back to Sherlock's mind Palace if  you will Thank You Julie for that I  hadn't really thought about that but  this is what it is it's really getting  to a place where you can actually  explore your data from the inside and  actually look at it from a digital  perspective so we are working right now  on something which we call the digital  twin this is not unique to us but the  digital twin is taking the physical  world and in real time digitizing it so  that artificial intelligence algorithms  can actually be looking at the physical  world through thi